## What was changed

- The other 19 skills in the upstream plugin were not taken. Several of them
  (`to-spec`, `to-tickets`, `implement`, `triage`, `wayfinder`) require a configured
  issue tracker via upstream's `setup-matt-pocock-skills`, which this plugin does not ship.
- Each skill's `agents/openai.yaml` was removed. It is Codex packaging metadata and is
  unused by Claude Code.
- Upstream's `node_modules/` (21 MB of authoring tooling) was not taken.
- `skills/tdd/SKILL.md` had its cross-reference to `codebase-design` namespaced to
  `engineering-kit:codebase-design`, because a skill shipped inside a plugin is addressed as
  `plugin:skill`. This is the only edit to a skill body; everything else is unmodified from
  upstream at the version above.

If you want these skills as their author ships them, with updates as he publishes them,
install the upstream plugin instead:

```
/plugin install mattpocock-skills
```

Installing both leaves you with every skill twice.
